{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Incomplete Retrieval of Recent Events\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"The system failed to retrieve critical memories from the memory bank that were stored but not returned to the generator. This often occurs with recent session data or updates that haven't been prioritized by the retrieval mechanism.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        \"Case 2\",\n        \"Case 5\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Imprecise Temporal and Entity Representation\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"Retrieved memories rely on relative time references (e.g., 'last week', 'yesterday') or implicit metadata (timestamps) rather than explicit absolute dates. The model struggles to resolve these relative references into specific calendar dates required by the question.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        \"Case 1\",\n        \"Case 3\",\n        \"Case 4\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Incomplete Retrieval of Recent Events\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Implement a recency-biased re-ranking strategy for retrieved memories to ensure the most recent session data and updates are prioritized. Additionally, enforce immediate indexing of new session transcripts into the memory bank before query processing begins.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Imprecise Temporal and Entity Representation\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Introduce a pre-processing step that normalizes relative temporal expressions (e.g., converting 'last week' to absolute dates based on the session timestamp) and extracts key entities (locations, names, counts) into structured fields alongside the raw text memory.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n- Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n- Keep each item concise and specific.\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory. Enforces temporal normalization (relative to absolute dates) and explicit entity extraction to improve retrieval precision.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nProcessing Steps:\\n1. Analyze the input text for temporal expressions (e.g., 'last week', 'tomorrow'). Normalize all relative times to absolute dates (YYYY-MM-DD) based on the current session context.\\n2. Identify and extract key entities (person names, locations, organizations, quantities) relevant to the fact.\\n3. Synthesize the memory content to include these normalized dates and extracted entities explicitly.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Select the appropriate action (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, NOOP).\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories unless correcting critical errors (prefer NOOP over incorrect updates).\\n- Output MUST follow the specific format below.\\n\\nOutput Format:\\nACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <content to store> (For INSERT only)\\nMEMORY_INDEX: <index> (For UPDATE/DELETE only)\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: <new content> (For UPDATE only)\\nREASONING: <why this action>\\n\\nIf uncertain about temporal normalization, infer the most logical absolute date based on session start time.\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory. Enforces temporal normalization and entity extraction to ensure precise retrieval.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Enriched)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- Prioritize immediate processing of recent session updates to ensure indexing.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Scan for new facts and plan details missing in memory.\\n2. Normalize relative time expressions (e.g., \\\\\\\"last week\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"tomorrow\\\\\\\") to absolute calendar dates based on the current session timestamp.\\n3. Extract key entities (names, locations, quantities) and include them clearly in the fact statement.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise, specific, and containing absolute temporal data.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Only output valid memory items that meet the enrichment criteria.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nRequired Output Format:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized_content_with_absolute_dates>\\nREASONING: <explanation_of_why_this_memory_is_added>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring precise temporal and entity normalization to support accurate retrieval.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert Structured Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring precise temporal and entity normalization to support accurate retrieval.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Identify all relative time references (e.g., 'last week', 'yesterday'). Convert these to absolute calendar dates (YYYY-MM-DD) based on the session timestamp before writing the memory.\\n2. Entity Extraction: Explicitly identify key entities (names, locations, counts) and include them in the memory summary.\\n3. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n4. Keep each item concise and specific.\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not output relative time references in the final memory item.\\nAction Format Requirements:\\nYou MUST output your decision in the following exact format:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized fact with absolute dates>\\nREASONING: <why this fact is stored and how time was resolved>\\nDo not output any other text besides the required fields.\\n\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.24888888888888888, 0.16, 0.16, 0.0]}

