{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The system successfully retrieves conversations containing relative time references (e.g., 'last night', 'next month', 'last Friday') but fails to perform the necessary temporal reasoning to convert these into absolute dates relative to the conversation timestamp. Consequently, it defaults to 'unknown' or vague responses.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Implement a temporal normalization module that parses conversation timestamps and relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month') to generate absolute dates before passing context to the generator. Additionally, use Chain-of-Thought prompting to force the model to explicitly calculate the date before answering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Contextual Disambiguation Failure\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        3,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The system struggles to distinguish between past aspirations/dreams and current factual events, or fails to prioritize specific details over vague summaries. It often conflates earlier memories (e.g., 'dream of visiting') with later confirmed actions (e.g., 'went to'), leading to hallucinated timeframes like 'sometime last year'.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Adjust retrieval scoring mechanisms to prioritize factual statements (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined') over aspirational ones (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to'). Train the generator to verify the tense and certainty of retrieved facts against the query requirements.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"Integrate a dedicated temporal reasoning layer that normalizes relative time expressions to absolute dates based on the conversation metadata.\",\n    \"Enhance retrieval ranking algorithms to weigh factual assertions higher than hypothetical or past-tense aspirations to prevent semantic confusion.\",\n    \"Adopt Chain-of-Thought prompting strategies that require the model to explicitly extract and validate temporal and factual constraints before generating the final answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, entity extraction, and factual disambiguation.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Enhanced)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nProcess Steps (Chain-of-Thought):\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Analyze for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month'). Convert all to absolute calendar dates using the session timestamp. Store absolute dates only.\\n2. Factual Verification: Distinguish between CONFIRMED FACTS (e.g., 'I went', 'I did') and ASPIRATIONS/HYPOTHESES (e.g., 'I plan to', 'I dream of'). Only store CONFIRMED FACTS.\\n3. Entity Extraction: Extract key entities (names, locations, counts) for precision.\\n4. Duplicate Check: Compare against existing memories to avoid redundancy.\\n5. Decision: If valid, proceed to INSERT. If no valid fact found or purely aspirational, proceed to NOOP.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT or NOOP only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT/NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>  (Required for INSERT)\\nMEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (Not applicable for INSERT)\\nREASONING: <explain why this action>\\n\\nExample INSERT Output:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: User visited Paris on 2023-10-26 via flight BA123.\\nMEMORY_INDEX: N/A\\nREASONING: Confirmed travel event with normalized date.\\n\\nExample NOOP Output:\\nACTION: NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: N/A\\nREASONING: Text contained only future plans without confirmation.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, fact-versus-aspiration disambiguation, and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed/factual rather than purely hypothetical or aspirational.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. CALCULATION STEP: Convert ALL relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. DISAMBIGUATION STEP: Verify if the statement describes a confirmed FACT (e.g., 'went', 'joined') or an ASPIRATION (e.g., 'dream', 'plan'). Prioritize confirmed facts for insertion. If only aspirational content exists, consider skipping or marking clearly as unconfirmed in the reasoning.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including time calculation and fact verification>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX and UPDATED_MEMORY are not applicable for INSERT actions.\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Ensure the MEMORY_ITEM contains absolute dates (YYYY-MM-DD) derived from Step 2.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, factual verification (fact vs. aspiration), and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed (not merely planned or dreamed).\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for potential memories.\\n2. **Temporal Normalization:** Locate any relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month'). Calculate their absolute calendar dates based on the current session timestamp.\\n3. **Factual Verification:** Distinguish between confirmed facts (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined') and aspirations (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to'). Prioritize confirmed facts. Skip pure speculation unless it represents a concrete, actionable plan.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below exactly.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nMEMORY_INDEX: null\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: null\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including the intermediate calculation for any converted time references>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and factual disambiguation.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory with Temporal and Factual Verification\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable, and verified facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed as factual (not a dream, plan, or hypothesis).\\n\\nHow to apply (Steps):\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Identify any relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next week'). Calculate the corresponding absolute calendar date based on the current conversation timestamp. Write down this calculation in your reasoning.\\n2. Factual Disambiguation: Verify the tense and modality of the statement. Do NOT store aspirational content (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to', 'might go'). Only store confirmed past or present facts (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined', 'is').\\n3. Entity Extraction: Extract key entities (locations, names) to integrate into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Duplicate Check: Compare against existing memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Output Generation: Generate the action using the required structure below.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, speculative, or unconfirmed content.\\n- Do not create new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including the date calculation and factual verification>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}

