{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"description\": \"The system fails to correctly interpret relative time expressions (e.g., 'last week', 'next month') in relation to the conversation timestamp, leading to vague or incorrect date predictions.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"In Case 1, 'last week' relative to June 21 should yield mid-June. In Case 5, 'next month' relative to Jan 7 should yield Feb. The model either ignored the timestamp or failed to calculate the offset.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Multi-Turn Fact Aggregation Failure\",\n      \"description\": \"The system struggles to aggregate discrete facts mentioned across multiple separate conversation sessions to form a complete answer (e.g., counting total items/people).\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"Andrew's pets (Toby, Buddy, Scout) were introduced in three different sessions (July, Oct, Nov). The retrieved memories contained all names, but the model failed to synthesize the count into 'three'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Low Confidence on Explicit Evidence\",\n      \"description\": \"The system predicts uncertainty ('unknown', 'not sure') even when the answer is explicitly stated in the retrieved context, indicating a lack of confidence calibration or attention to the provided text.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        2,\n        3,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"In Case 3, the text states 'I finally opened my own car maintenance shop' on May 1. The model claimed 'not sure'. In Case 2, 'last night' is explicit, yet the model said 'unknown'.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Implement a dedicated temporal normalization module that parses conversation timestamps alongside relative date phrases (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month') to generate absolute dates before passing context to the QA generator.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Add a pre-processing step that converts all relative time mentions in the retrieved memory snippets to ISO format dates based on the session header timestamp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Multi-Turn Fact Aggregation Failure\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Introduce a Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning requirement for questions involving counts or cumulative facts, forcing the model to list entities found in each retrieved memory chunk before summing them.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Modify the prompt to instruct the model: 'List all instances of [entity] found in the retrieved memories, then provide the total count.'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Low Confidence on Explicit Evidence\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Train the model to prioritize explicit textual evidence over internal priors by implementing an 'Evidence Citation' constraint in the generation prompt.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Require the model to output the specific sentence from the retrieved memory that supports its answer. If no sentence is found, then allow 'unknown'; otherwise, force a definitive answer.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts with strict temporal normalization and explicit evidence citation to reduce ambiguity and increase confidence.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Identify the session timestamp provided in the header.\\n2. Locate any relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week') in the text chunk.\\n3. Calculate the absolute date by applying the offset to the session timestamp. Write out the calculation logic (e.g., 'June 21 - 7 days = June 14') in your reasoning.\\n4. Extract key entities and integrate them into the memory content.\\n5. Locate the exact sentence in the text chunk that contains the core fact. Include a direct quote of this sentence in your reasoning to ground the decision.\\n6. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n7. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n8. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <calculate date difference here AND quote source text here>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Enhanced memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, entity enumeration, and evidence citation to prevent temporal reasoning and aggregation failures.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Extract the conversation session timestamp. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates (ISO format) using the session timestamp BEFORE generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and list ALL instances found in the text chunk to support future aggregation.\\n4. Identify the specific sentence in the text that serves as evidence for the memory fact.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, NOOP).\\n- You must output the action using the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\n\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates, entity lists, and evidence citation>\\nREASONING: <List entities found, explain temporal conversion, cite evidence snippet>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\\n\\nExample Output:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: User opened car maintenance shop on 2023-05-01. Evidence: \\\"I finally opened my own car maintenance shop\\\".\\nREASONING: Entities: ['car maintenance shop']. Time converted from 'May 1' using session date. Evidence cited from text.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced strict temporal normalization and entity extraction to prevent relative time representation errors.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Parse the current session timestamp from the input metadata.\\n2. Identify all relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week', 'next month') in the text chunk.\\n3. Calculate absolute dates for these expressions based on the session timestamp. STRICTLY replace relative terms with absolute dates (ISO 8601 format) in the memory content.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- OUTPUT FORMAT: You must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nMEMORY_INDEX: N/A\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: N/A\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts with enforced temporal normalization, entity aggregation, and explicit evidence citation to prevent reasoning deficits and confidence failures.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert Enhanced Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring high-quality storage for downstream retrieval.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. **Temporal Normalization:** Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates (ISO format YYYY-MM-DD) using the current session timestamp BEFORE generating the memory content.\\n3. **Entity Aggregation:** If multiple instances of an entity are mentioned (e.g., pets, locations), aggregate them into a single list within the memory item to facilitate multi-turn counting.\\n4. **Evidence Citation:** Preserve explicit quotes or specific details from the text that support the fact within the memory content to improve retrieval confidence.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <absolute_date normalized content with aggregated lists and explicit quotes>\\nREASONING: <confirm temporal conversion and evidence preservation>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}

