{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Incomplete Retrieval of Recent Events\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"The system failed to retrieve critical memories from the memory bank that were stored but not returned to the generator. This often occurs with recent session data or updates that haven't been prioritized by the retrieval mechanism.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        \"Case 2\",\n        \"Case 5\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Imprecise Temporal and Entity Representation\",\n      \"root_cause\": \"Retrieved memories rely on relative time references (e.g., 'last week', 'yesterday') or implicit metadata (timestamps) rather than explicit absolute dates. The model struggles to resolve these relative references into specific calendar dates required by the question.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        \"Case 1\",\n        \"Case 3\",\n        \"Case 4\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Incomplete Retrieval of Recent Events\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Implement a recency-biased re-ranking strategy for retrieved memories to ensure the most recent session data and updates are prioritized. Additionally, enforce immediate indexing of new session transcripts into the memory bank before query processing begins.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Imprecise Temporal and Entity Representation\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Introduce a pre-processing step that normalizes relative temporal expressions (e.g., converting 'last week' to absolute dates based on the session timestamp) and extracts key entities (locations, names, counts) into structured fields alongside the raw text memory.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n- Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n- Keep each item concise and specific.\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory. Enforces temporal normalization (relative to absolute dates) and explicit entity extraction to improve retrieval precision.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nProcessing Steps:\\n1. Analyze the input text for temporal expressions (e.g., 'last week', 'tomorrow'). Normalize all relative times to absolute dates (YYYY-MM-DD) based on the current session context.\\n2. Identify and extract key entities (person names, locations, organizations, quantities) relevant to the fact.\\n3. Synthesize the memory content to include these normalized dates and extracted entities explicitly.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Select the appropriate action (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, NOOP).\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories unless correcting critical errors (prefer NOOP over incorrect updates).\\n- Output MUST follow the specific format below.\\n\\nOutput Format:\\nACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <content to store> (For INSERT only)\\nMEMORY_INDEX: <index> (For UPDATE/DELETE only)\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: <new content> (For UPDATE only)\\nREASONING: <why this action>\\n\\nIf uncertain about temporal normalization, infer the most logical absolute date based on session start time.\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory. Enforces temporal normalization and entity extraction to ensure precise retrieval.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Enriched)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- Prioritize immediate processing of recent session updates to ensure indexing.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Scan for new facts and plan details missing in memory.\\n2. Normalize relative time expressions (e.g., \\\\\\\"last week\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"tomorrow\\\\\\\") to absolute calendar dates based on the current session timestamp.\\n3. Extract key entities (names, locations, quantities) and include them clearly in the fact statement.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise, specific, and containing absolute temporal data.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Only output valid memory items that meet the enrichment criteria.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nRequired Output Format:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized_content_with_absolute_dates>\\nREASONING: <explanation_of_why_this_memory_is_added>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring precise temporal and entity normalization to support accurate retrieval.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert Structured Memory\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring precise temporal and entity normalization to support accurate retrieval.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Identify all relative time references (e.g., 'last week', 'yesterday'). Convert these to absolute calendar dates (YYYY-MM-DD) based on the session timestamp before writing the memory.\\n2. Entity Extraction: Explicitly identify key entities (names, locations, counts) and include them in the memory summary.\\n3. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n4. Keep each item concise and specific.\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not output relative time references in the final memory item.\\nAction Format Requirements:\\nYou MUST output your decision in the following exact format:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized fact with absolute dates>\\nREASONING: <why this fact is stored and how time was resolved>\\nDo not output any other text besides the required fields.\\n\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.24888888888888888, 0.16, 0.16, 0.0]}
{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The system successfully retrieves conversations containing relative time references (e.g., 'last night', 'next month', 'last Friday') but fails to perform the necessary temporal reasoning to convert these into absolute dates relative to the conversation timestamp. Consequently, it defaults to 'unknown' or vague responses.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Implement a temporal normalization module that parses conversation timestamps and relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month') to generate absolute dates before passing context to the generator. Additionally, use Chain-of-Thought prompting to force the model to explicitly calculate the date before answering.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Contextual Disambiguation Failure\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        3,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The system struggles to distinguish between past aspirations/dreams and current factual events, or fails to prioritize specific details over vague summaries. It often conflates earlier memories (e.g., 'dream of visiting') with later confirmed actions (e.g., 'went to'), leading to hallucinated timeframes like 'sometime last year'.\",\n      \"recommendation\": \"Adjust retrieval scoring mechanisms to prioritize factual statements (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined') over aspirational ones (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to'). Train the generator to verify the tense and certainty of retrieved facts against the query requirements.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    \"Integrate a dedicated temporal reasoning layer that normalizes relative time expressions to absolute dates based on the conversation metadata.\",\n    \"Enhance retrieval ranking algorithms to weigh factual assertions higher than hypothetical or past-tense aspirations to prevent semantic confusion.\",\n    \"Adopt Chain-of-Thought prompting strategies that require the model to explicitly extract and validate temporal and factual constraints before generating the final answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, entity extraction, and factual disambiguation.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Enhanced)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nProcess Steps (Chain-of-Thought):\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Analyze for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month'). Convert all to absolute calendar dates using the session timestamp. Store absolute dates only.\\n2. Factual Verification: Distinguish between CONFIRMED FACTS (e.g., 'I went', 'I did') and ASPIRATIONS/HYPOTHESES (e.g., 'I plan to', 'I dream of'). Only store CONFIRMED FACTS.\\n3. Entity Extraction: Extract key entities (names, locations, counts) for precision.\\n4. Duplicate Check: Compare against existing memories to avoid redundancy.\\n5. Decision: If valid, proceed to INSERT. If no valid fact found or purely aspirational, proceed to NOOP.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT or NOOP only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT/NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>  (Required for INSERT)\\nMEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (Not applicable for INSERT)\\nREASONING: <explain why this action>\\n\\nExample INSERT Output:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: User visited Paris on 2023-10-26 via flight BA123.\\nMEMORY_INDEX: N/A\\nREASONING: Confirmed travel event with normalized date.\\n\\nExample NOOP Output:\\nACTION: NOOP\\nMEMORY_ITEM: N/A\\nREASONING: Text contained only future plans without confirmation.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, fact-versus-aspiration disambiguation, and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed/factual rather than purely hypothetical or aspirational.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. CALCULATION STEP: Convert ALL relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. DISAMBIGUATION STEP: Verify if the statement describes a confirmed FACT (e.g., 'went', 'joined') or an ASPIRATION (e.g., 'dream', 'plan'). Prioritize confirmed facts for insertion. If only aspirational content exists, consider skipping or marking clearly as unconfirmed in the reasoning.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including time calculation and fact verification>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX and UPDATED_MEMORY are not applicable for INSERT actions.\\n\\nIMPORTANT: Ensure the MEMORY_ITEM contains absolute dates (YYYY-MM-DD) derived from Step 2.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, factual verification (fact vs. aspiration), and entity extraction.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed (not merely planned or dreamed).\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for potential memories.\\n2. **Temporal Normalization:** Locate any relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month'). Calculate their absolute calendar dates based on the current session timestamp.\\n3. **Factual Verification:** Distinguish between confirmed facts (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined') and aspirations (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to'). Prioritize confirmed facts. Skip pure speculation unless it represents a concrete, actionable plan.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below exactly.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nMEMORY_INDEX: null\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: null\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including the intermediate calculation for any converted time references>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and factual disambiguation.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory with Temporal and Factual Verification\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable, and verified facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n- The event is confirmed as factual (not a dream, plan, or hypothesis).\\n\\nHow to apply (Steps):\\n1. Temporal Normalization: Identify any relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next week'). Calculate the corresponding absolute calendar date based on the current conversation timestamp. Write down this calculation in your reasoning.\\n2. Factual Disambiguation: Verify the tense and modality of the statement. Do NOT store aspirational content (e.g., 'I dream of', 'I plan to', 'might go'). Only store confirmed past or present facts (e.g., 'I went', 'I joined', 'is').\\n3. Entity Extraction: Extract key entities (locations, names) to integrate into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Duplicate Check: Compare against existing memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Output Generation: Generate the action using the required structure below.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, speculative, or unconfirmed content.\\n- Do not create new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted, including the date calculation and factual verification>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}
{"prompt": "Based on the following analysis of failure cases, propose a specific skill improvement.\n\n## Analysis\n{\n  \"failure_patterns\": [\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"description\": \"The system fails to correctly interpret relative time expressions (e.g., 'last week', 'next month') in relation to the conversation timestamp, leading to vague or incorrect date predictions.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        1,\n        2,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"In Case 1, 'last week' relative to June 21 should yield mid-June. In Case 5, 'next month' relative to Jan 7 should yield Feb. The model either ignored the timestamp or failed to calculate the offset.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Multi-Turn Fact Aggregation Failure\",\n      \"description\": \"The system struggles to aggregate discrete facts mentioned across multiple separate conversation sessions to form a complete answer (e.g., counting total items/people).\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"Andrew's pets (Toby, Buddy, Scout) were introduced in three different sessions (July, Oct, Nov). The retrieved memories contained all names, but the model failed to synthesize the count into 'three'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"root_cause\": \"memory_quality_failure\",\n      \"pattern_name\": \"Low Confidence on Explicit Evidence\",\n      \"description\": \"The system predicts uncertainty ('unknown', 'not sure') even when the answer is explicitly stated in the retrieved context, indicating a lack of confidence calibration or attention to the provided text.\",\n      \"affected_cases\": [\n        2,\n        3,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"example_analysis\": \"In Case 3, the text states 'I finally opened my own car maintenance shop' on May 1. The model claimed 'not sure'. In Case 2, 'last night' is explicit, yet the model said 'unknown'.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendations\": [\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Temporal Reasoning Deficit\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Implement a dedicated temporal normalization module that parses conversation timestamps alongside relative date phrases (e.g., 'yesterday', 'next month') to generate absolute dates before passing context to the QA generator.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Add a pre-processing step that converts all relative time mentions in the retrieved memory snippets to ISO format dates based on the session header timestamp.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Multi-Turn Fact Aggregation Failure\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Introduce a Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning requirement for questions involving counts or cumulative facts, forcing the model to list entities found in each retrieved memory chunk before summing them.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Modify the prompt to instruct the model: 'List all instances of [entity] found in the retrieved memories, then provide the total count.'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_pattern\": \"Low Confidence on Explicit Evidence\",\n      \"skill_change\": \"Train the model to prioritize explicit textual evidence over internal priors by implementing an 'Evidence Citation' constraint in the generation prompt.\",\n      \"implementation_detail\": \"Require the model to output the specific sentence from the retrieved memory that supports its answer. If no sentence is found, then allow 'unknown'; otherwise, force a definitive answer.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n## Current Skills\n[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"insert\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization and entity extraction.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates using the current session timestamp before generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content for precision.\\n4. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n5. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n6. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n    \"update_type\": \"insert\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"update\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for revising an existing memory item when the text chunk provides corrections or new details.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Update Existing Memory\\nPurpose: Revise a retrieved memory with new or corrected information from the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clarifies, corrects, or extends a retrieved memory.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Select the best matching memory item.\\n- Merge new details into a single updated item.\\n- Preserve accurate details that still hold.\\nConstraints:\\n- Do not create new memories.\\n- Do not delete items.\\nAction type: UPDATE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"update\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"delete\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for removing memory items that are incorrect, outdated, or superseded.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Delete Invalid Memory\\nPurpose: Remove a retrieved memory that is wrong, outdated, or superseded by the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk clearly contradicts a memory.\\n- A plan or fact is explicitly canceled or replaced.\\nHow to apply:\\n- Only delete when evidence is explicit.\\nConstraints:\\n- If uncertain, prefer no action over deletion.\\nAction type: DELETE only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"delete\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noop\",\n    \"description\": \"Memory management skill for confirming that no memory changes are required.\",\n    \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: No Operation\\nPurpose: Confirm no memory changes are needed for the text chunk.\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk contains no new, corrective, or actionable information.\\nConstraints:\\n- Emit NOOP only if none of the selected skills produce actions.\\nAction type: NOOP only.\\n\",\n    \"update_type\": \"noop\",\n    \"meta_info\": {\n      \"usage_count\": 0,\n      \"avg_reward\": 0.0,\n      \"recent_rewards\": [],\n      \"recent_usage_ema\": 0.0,\n      \"created_at\": \"initial\",\n      \"last_modified\": \"initial\"\n    },\n    \"embedding\": null\n  }\n]\n\n## Instructions\nPropose ONE concrete skill change. Output JSON with:\n- \"action\": \"add_new\" or \"refine\"\n- \"target_skill\": skill name to refine (or null for add_new)\n- \"name\": skill name\n- \"description\": what the skill does\n- \"instruction_template\": the LLM instruction template for this skill\n- \"update_type\": \"insert\" or \"update\" or \"delete\"\n\n## CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS for instruction_template:\n1. The skill's instruction_template MUST instruct the executor to output actions using ONLY these standard action types: INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, or NOOP.\n2. The executor output format MUST follow this structure:\n   ACTION: INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE/NOOP\n   MEMORY_ITEM: <content to store>  (for INSERT)\n   MEMORY_INDEX: <index>  (for UPDATE/DELETE)\n   UPDATED_MEMORY: <new content>  (for UPDATE)\n   REASONING: <why this action>\n3. Do NOT invent new action types (e.g., no \"STRUCTURE_AND_ENRICH\", no \"PRE-PROCESSING\").\n4. Any preprocessing logic (temporal normalization, fact extraction, etc.) should be described as STEPS within the skill that produce a final INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE action — not as a separate action type.\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON.", "responses": ["{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts with strict temporal normalization and explicit evidence citation to reduce ambiguity and increase confidence.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory (Refined)\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Identify the session timestamp provided in the header.\\n2. Locate any relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week') in the text chunk.\\n3. Calculate the absolute date by applying the offset to the session timestamp. Write out the calculation logic (e.g., 'June 21 - 7 days = June 14') in your reasoning.\\n4. Extract key entities and integrate them into the memory content.\\n5. Locate the exact sentence in the text chunk that contains the core fact. Include a direct quote of this sentence in your reasoning to ground the decision.\\n6. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n7. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n8. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nREASONING: <calculate date difference here AND quote source text here>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Enhanced memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced temporal normalization, entity enumeration, and evidence citation to prevent temporal reasoning and aggregation failures.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. Extract the conversation session timestamp. Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates (ISO format) using the session timestamp BEFORE generating the memory content.\\n3. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and list ALL instances found in the text chunk to support future aggregation.\\n4. Identify the specific sentence in the text that serves as evidence for the memory fact.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types (INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, NOOP).\\n- You must output the action using the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\n\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates, entity lists, and evidence citation>\\nREASONING: <List entities found, explain temporal conversion, cite evidence snippet>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\\n\\nExample Output:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: User opened car maintenance shop on 2023-05-01. Evidence: \\\"I finally opened my own car maintenance shop\\\".\\nREASONING: Entities: ['car maintenance shop']. Time converted from 'May 1' using session date. Evidence cited from text.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are not already in memory, with enforced strict temporal normalization and entity extraction to prevent relative time representation errors.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert New Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Parse the current session timestamp from the input metadata.\\n2. Identify all relative time expressions (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week', 'next month') in the text chunk.\\n3. Calculate absolute dates for these expressions based on the session timestamp. STRICTLY replace relative terms with absolute dates (ISO 8601 format) in the memory content.\\n4. Extract key entities (locations, names, counts) and integrate them into the memory content.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- OUTPUT FORMAT: You must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <normalized content with absolute dates and entities>\\nMEMORY_INDEX: N/A\\nUPDATED_MEMORY: N/A\\nREASONING: <explain why this fact was inserted>\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}", "{\n  \"action\": \"refine\",\n  \"target_skill\": \"insert\",\n  \"name\": \"insert\",\n  \"description\": \"Memory management skill for capturing new, durable facts with enforced temporal normalization, entity aggregation, and explicit evidence citation to prevent reasoning deficits and confidence failures.\",\n  \"instruction_template\": \"Skill: Insert Enhanced Memory\\n\\nPurpose: Capture new, durable facts from the current text chunk that are missing in memory, ensuring high-quality storage for downstream retrieval.\\n\\nWhen to use:\\n- The text chunk introduces new facts, events, plans, or context worth storing.\\n- The information is stable and likely useful later.\\n\\nHow to apply:\\n1. Analyze the text chunk for relative time references (e.g., 'yesterday', 'last week').\\n2. **Temporal Normalization:** Convert all relative time references to absolute calendar dates (ISO format YYYY-MM-DD) using the current session timestamp BEFORE generating the memory content.\\n3. **Entity Aggregation:** If multiple instances of an entity are mentioned (e.g., pets, locations), aggregate them into a single list within the memory item to facilitate multi-turn counting.\\n4. **Evidence Citation:** Preserve explicit quotes or specific details from the text that support the fact within the memory content to improve retrieval confidence.\\n5. Compare against retrieved memories to avoid duplicates.\\n6. Split distinct facts into separate items.\\n7. Keep each item concise and specific.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n- Skip trivial, fleeting, or speculative content.\\n- Do not update or delete existing memories.\\n- Do not invent new action types; use only STANDARD action types.\\n- Output MUST follow the required structure below.\\n\\nAction type: INSERT only.\\n\\nOutput Format Requirements:\\nYou must output your decision in the following exact structure:\\nACTION: INSERT\\nMEMORY_ITEM: <absolute_date normalized content with aggregated lists and explicit quotes>\\nREASONING: <confirm temporal conversion and evidence preservation>\\nNOTE: MEMORY_INDEX is not applicable for INSERT actions.\",\n  \"update_type\": \"insert\"\n}"], "rewards": [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]}
